  "query_preview": "..\nThe trade-wind regime will continue for the Marianas, promoting\nperiods of isolated showers with limited convection due to a \ntemperature inversion and drier mid-level air stifling vertical \ngrowth. There may be potential for a brief period of low-end scattered\nshowers on Friday, but deterministic and ensemble accumulated \nprecipitation are leaning towards isolated. According to the U.S. \nDrought Monitor, there is no indication of drought occurring in the\nMarianas. However, little to no rainfall over the past several weeks\nshould not be overlooked as total rainfall amounts at this time of \nyear are about 3 inches below normal. As such, water conservation \nefforts are encouraged as dry season approaches, which could \npotentially introduce abnormally dry (D0) conditions across the \nregion.",
